# Personal campus data stays visible at ./studies but must never enter source control.
# The leading slash is load-bearing: an unanchored `studies/` matches a directory
# of that name at any depth, and this repository has a source module at
# server/studies/. Without the anchor Git silently swallowed it, and a fresh
# clone could not build.
/studies/

# Session handoff notes — working material, not project documentation.
.handoff/

# Quality-loop working material: screenshots, evidence dumps, and handoff notes
# produced while investigating a session's findings. The path says `tmp` because
# it is — the durable outcome is a learning under docs/reference/learnings/.
/artifacts/**/tmp/
